---
# ORDER MATTERS: the validating webhook rejects overlapping pools, and `kubectl apply` goes in file
# order, so homelab-pool must narrow FIRST or ingress-pool is denied.
# autoAssign: false is what keeps ordinary Services off the ingress address.
apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: IPAddressPool
metadata:
  name: homelab-pool
  namespace: metallb-system
spec:
  addresses:
    - {{ k3s_metallb_pool }}
---
apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: IPAddressPool
metadata:
  name: ingress-pool
  namespace: metallb-system
spec:
  addresses:
    - {{ k3s_metallb_ingress_vip }}/32
  autoAssign: false
---
apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: L2Advertisement
metadata:
  name: homelab-l2
  namespace: metallb-system
spec:
  ipAddressPools:
    - ingress-pool
    - homelab-pool
  # Announce VIPs from daniel-box ONLY: when daniel-server's speaker wins the L2 election for
  # 10.0.0.240, every Docker container on that host loses the cluster, because a Docker-bridge
  # client cannot reach a VIP its own host announces (the hairpin class).
  # PERMANENT (operator decision, design.md §10 #6): with ETP Local load-bearing
  # for client-IP preservation and two asymmetric nodes, this pin and the VIP-backed
  # workloads' daniel-box nodeSelectors are one unit — never move either alone.
  #
  # THE FULL SET: traefik, pihole, mosquitto, terraria, valheim, wg-easy, and jellyfin. Jellyfin
  # is the odd one out: it is pinned here by the
  # media-volume `local` PV's required nodeAffinity rather than by its own nodeSelector, so
  # jellyfin-lan's VIP is safe only for as long as that volume stays node-local.
  #
  # ANY NEW `type: LoadBalancer` SERVICE WITH externalTrafficPolicy: Local NEEDS A PIN HERE.
  # The failure is silent: the pod reports healthy on the wrong node while its VIP drops
  # every packet. `kubectl get svc -A | grep LoadBalancer` is the census.
  #
  # DECIDED: `k8s_primary_node`, not the literal `daniel-box` it read until 2026-08-27. The
  # workload pins this must stay in step with are all that variable already, and a literal
  # here was the last way the two halves could drift apart. It also lets a single-node
  # staging cluster announce from its own node instead of naming prod's.
  nodeSelectors:
    - matchLabels:
        kubernetes.io/hostname: {{ k8s_primary_node }}
